# Wave 23: the reference measurement JSON is hashed by check_fixtures.py and is
# committed with LF; Windows CI has core.autocrlf=true, which converted it to
# CRLF on checkout and failed the fixture gate (run 39945123565).  Pin THIS file
# to LF.  Do not blanket-normalise the tree: project_a_recalc_golden.tsv is
# committed with CRLF and its documented SHA-256 is of those bytes.
tests/data/reference/*.json text eol=lf
*.mpp binary
*.png binary
*.bin binary

# Wave 33 (W33-4.2, audit C-3): the wave-32 merge commits reintroduced CRLF in
# three files, undoing W32-C1.  Source and record types are pinned to LF on
# every checkout and CI fails on a CR in them (ci.yml).  The grandfathered
# .tsv/.json/.txt files are deliberately NOT typed here: several have documented
# SHA-256s of their CRLF bytes.
*.md text=auto eol=lf
*.py text=auto eol=lf
*.yml text=auto eol=lf
*.cpp text=auto eol=lf
*.h text=auto eol=lf
